e obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-2$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means  \n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2+1-1=-2.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186342135 :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=30,$ then $\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3}u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v)}=$" "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=30,$ then $\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3}u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v)}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186342136 :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=27,$ then $\\frac{(2u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (3v)}=$" "If $u=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=27,$ then $\\frac{(2u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (3v)}=$"] [:db/cas 17592186342138 :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$"] [:db/cas 17592186342138 :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=5.$ Substituting this value in the second and first equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{2}-2(5)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{1}+5=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=5,$ which means \n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+4+5=12.\n$$" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -14\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 